data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_07362c2bc60de9ba006aa882a4834887d09e852cedbf618c7e","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":140,"text":"On September 13, 2026, leaders from major AI labs—including Anthropic, SpaceXAI, OpenAI, and Google DeepMind—united to advocate for a slowdown in AI development. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei initiated this call, expressing concerns that rapid AI progress could lead to catastrophic scenarios within six months. His remarks were echoed by top executives, including Elon Musk, Sam Altman, and Demis Hassabis, who emphasized prioritizing safety over growth. This rare moment of unity within the competitive industry reflects growing public concern and legislative pressures regarding unchecked AI development. ([axios.com](https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-am-68956162-ed74-42e1-a892-ae3da8e7d74f?utm_source=openai))\n\n\n## Highlights:\n- [🚦 Axios AM: Hitting AI brakes](https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-am-68956162-ed74-42e1-a892-ae3da8e7d74f?utm_source=openai), Published on Sunday, September 13 "}

